  "tolerance_note": "Every numeric quantity carries its own tolerance; lengths are in metres in the IFC project coordinate system (no georeferencing). Coordinate tolerances are 1 mm (1e-3 m), the accuracy a viewer needs; the independent integration itself is good to about 1e-9 m.",
  "computation": {
    "horizontal": "x(s) = integral of cos(heading(t)) dt from 0 to s, y(s) = integral of sin(heading(t)) dt; heading comes from the clothoid/arc/line design parameters. Composite 8-point Gauss-Legendre, intervals <= 10 m, estimated error < 1e-9 m; checked against the closed-form clothoid power series and the mirrored R->infinity clothoid identity. Nothing here uses IfcOpenShell geometry.",
    "vertical": "z(s) = integral of the piecewise gradient; constant gradients integrate to lines, the parabolic arc to a quadratic. Closed form, no numeric error.",
    "cant": "Cant is authored as IfcAlignmentCant + IfcAlignmentCantSegment with a rail head distance of 1.5 m. Values are rail heights over the vertical alignment per IFC 4.3: the left rail rises from 0 to 0.04 m and back to 0, the right rail stays at 0. The kernel is expected to report cant as ignored; the expected x/y/z below are the plain horizontal/vertical centreline and contain no cant contribution. The cant_left_ignored / cant_right_ignored fields document the authored data only."
  },
  "expected_kernel_behaviour": {
    "cant": "ignored (report the IfcAlignmentCant data as unsupported/ignored); geometry must equal the horizontal + vertical alignment without any transverse rotation.",
    "max_cant_angle_if_applied": {
      "value": 0.026660348374597954,
      "unit": "rad",
      "tolerance": 1e-12,
      "note": "atan((left-right)/rail head distance) in the constant 0.04 m section; informational only"
    }
  },
